# AGENTS.md - Generic Agent Charter

Any skill-aware agent that respects an `AGENTS.md` convention (Cursor, Continue.dev, Hermes, and others) should load this file as its charter when operating inside this vault.

Replace `<ANGLE_BRACKET>` placeholders before first use.

---

## The vault

- Owner: `<YOUR_NAME>`
- Root: `<YOUR_VAULT_ROOT>`
- Purpose: personal second brain. Markdown only. Local-first. No sync without owner consent.

---

## Default voice

Operational unless the owner asks for long-form.

- Lead with the point. Active voice. Short sentences.
- No em dashes, no prose semicolons.
- No AI vocabulary. Specifically avoid: delve, leverage, utilize, robust, seamless, moreover, furthermore.
- No streak-shaming, no productivity-coach phrasing. The vault owner may have ADHD. Treat the system as a tool, not a scoreboard.

---

## Folder map

| Folder | Role | Agent permission |
|---|---|---|
| `00-Inbox/` | Capture zone | Read only unless owner approves write for a specific batch |
| `01-Daily-Notes/` | Dated journal | Append only |
| `02-People/` | One note per person | Full |
| `03-Projects/` | Active work | Full |
| `04-Areas/` | Ongoing responsibilities | Full |
| `05-Resources/` | Reference material | Full |
| `06-Archive/` | Retired content | Append only |
| `07-Attachments/` | Binaries | Full with no deletion |
| `08-AI/` | Agent session logs | Full |
| `09-Dreams/` | Optional dream log | Append only |
| `10-Study/` | Optional domain knowledge | Full |
| `99-MOC/` | Maps of content | Full |
| `99-System/` | Templates and scripts | Full with no deletion of scripts without ask |
| `Legacy/` | Family-only material | Hard off limits |

---

## Linking rules

- Use `[[wikilinks]]`. Prefer links to tags for structural connections.
- Create a stub when a wikilink points nowhere, mark it `status/draft`, and surface it to the owner.

---

## Session hygiene

Write a short session log to `08-AI/YYYY-MM-DD_<agent-name>_session.md` at the end of every working session. Include files touched, open threads, and one honest line about what went well.

---

## Hard rules

1. The `Legacy/` folder is off limits for all operations.
2. Never send vault content to external services beyond the model reading this file.
3. Never commit files with `private` in the filename.
4. Never fabricate quotes, citations, numbers, or dates.
5. Ask one clarifying question when intent is ambiguous. Do not guess.

